4 - e.$\n\nA tangent vector to the level curve that passes through the point $(1,e)$ can be computed as follows:\n\n$$\nt(1,e)=f_y(1,e)i-f_x(1,e)j\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(1,e):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(- x^{2} - x y - 3 x \\ln{\\left(y \\right)})\\,i-\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(- x^{2} - x y - 3 x \\ln{\\left(y \\right)})\\,j \\\\ &=(- x - \\frac{3 x}{y})\\,i-(- 2 x - y - 3 \\ln{\\left(y \\right)})\\,j \\\\ t(1,e)&=(- \\left(1\\right) - \\frac{3 \\left(1\\right)}{\\left(e\\right)})\\,i-(- 2 \\left(1\\right) - \\left(e\\right) - 3 \\ln{\\left(\\left(e\\right) \\right)})\\,j \\\\ &=(- \\frac{3}{e} - 1)\\,i-(-5 - e)\\,j \\\\ &=-\\left(1 + \\frac{3}{e}\\right)\\, i+\\left(e + 5\\right)\\, j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our tangent vector is $-\\left(1 + \\frac{3}{e}\\right)\\, i+\\left(e + 5\\right)\\, j.$" 13194139535907 17592186045443 true] [17592186540216 1068 #edb/ref 17592186540259 13194139535907 17592186045443 true] [17592186540216 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535907 17592186045443 true] [17592186540216 1071 "Consider the plane curve $- 3 x^{2} + 4 x y + 4 y=0.$ Find a tangent vector to that curve at the point $(2,1).$" 13194139535907 17592186045443 true] [17592186540216 1072 #uuid "382a9b70-c2b2-5746-b04d-f8a10b7cc350" 13194139535907 17592186045443 true] [17592186540216 1074 "First, if we set $f(x,y)=- 3 x^{2} + 4 x y + 4 y,$ our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$\n\nA tangent vector to the level curve that passes through the point $(2,1)$ can be computed as follows:\n\n$$\nt(2,1)=f_y(2,1)i-f_x(2,1)j\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(2,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(- 3 x^{2} + 4 x y + 4 y)\\,i-\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(- 3 x^{2} + 4 x y + 4 y)\\,j \\\\ &=(4 x + 4)\\,i-(- 6 x + 4 y)\\,j \\\\ t(2,1)&=(4 \\left(2\\right) + 4)\\,i-(- 6 \\left(2\\right) + 4 \\left(1\\right))\\,j \\\\ &=(12)\\,i-(-8)\\,j \\\\ &=12\\, i+8\\, j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our tangent vector is $12\\, i+8\\, j.$" 13194139535907 17592186045443 true] [17592186540217 1080 "\\left(\\frac{8}{e^{2}} + 2\\right)\\, i-\\left(4 + e^{2}\\right)\\, j" 13194139535907 17592186045443 true] [17592186540217 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535907 17592186045443 true] [17592186540217 1083 #uuid "3f09bec7-8ba4-511e-bb9e-4fdd3cfd1b47" 13194139535907 17592186045443 true] [17592186540218 1080 "\\left(11 - e\\right)\\, i-\\left(1 - \\frac{3}{e}\\right)\\, j" 13194139535907 17592186045443 true] [17592186540218 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535907 17592186045443 true] [17592186540218 1083 #uuid "46056d71-cea5-53af-8fdf-cff404969bbf" 13194139535907 17592186045443 true] [17592186540219 1068 #edb/ref 17592186540214 13194139535907 17592186045443 true] [17592186540219 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535907 17592186045443 true] [17592186540219 1071 "Consider the plane curve $4 x^{2} + x y - y=17.$ Find a tangent vector to that curve at the point $(2,1).$" 13194139535907 17592186045443 true] [17592186540219 1072 #uuid "4d7dfdec-ea45-55c1-8a36-f476d7f30b88" 13194139535907 17592186045443 true] [17592186540219 1074 "First, if we set $f(x,y)=4 x^{2} + x y - y,$ our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=17.$\n\nA tangent vector to the level curve that passes through the point $(2,1)$ can be computed as follows:\n\n$$\nt(2,1)=f_y(2,1)i-f_x(2,1)j\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(2,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(4 x^{2} + x y - y)\\,i-\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(4 x^{2} + x y - y)\\,j \\\\ &=(x - 1)\\,i-(8 x + y)\\,j \\\\ t(2,1)&=(\\left(2\\right) - 1)\\,i-(8 \\left(2\\right) + \\left(1\\right))\\,j \\\\ &=(1)\\,i-(17)\\,j \\\\ &=i-17\\, j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our tangent vector is $i-17\\, j.$" 13194139535907 17592186045443 true] [17592186540220 1080 "-\\left(1 + \\frac{3}{e}\\right)\\, i-\\left(e + 5\\right)\\, j" 13194139535907 1